{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1412114-contradiction-between-titanomachy-and-mysteries-of-the-world","id":1412114,"title":"Contradiction between Titanomachy and Mysteries of the World?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-05T10:55:19-07:00","id":1412114,"title":"Contradiction between Titanomachy and Mysteries of the World?","content":"In Mysteries of the World Belenus and Cernunnos are described as gods. In Titanomachy they\u2019re described as Titans. I\u2019m confused. Are these two different beings with the same name or is this just supposed to point out how the line is blurry between gods and Titans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T10:56:39-07:00","id":1412115,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s two different beings who share the same name","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24769-magicjohnny","name":"Magicjohnny","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24769_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:10:46-07:00","id":1412119,"title":"","content":"I was pretty sure that was the case for Cernunnos. But there are two different beings named Belenus too? One god, one Titan? I read the entry in Titanomachy really carefully and it doesn\u2019t say for sure. Did Belenus become a Titan after his pantheon was destroyed by Julius Caesar and the Theoi?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:18:20-07:00","id":1412120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1412114-contradiction-between-titanomachy-and-mysteries-of-the-world?p=1412119#post1412119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was pretty sure that was the case for Cernunnos. But there are two different beings named Belenus too? One god, one Titan? I read the entry in Titanomachy really carefully and it doesn\u2019t say for sure. Did Belenus become a Titan after his pantheon was destroyed by Julius Caesar and the Theoi?</div> </div> </div> </div>It appears that there will be a number of such double beings (Cernunnos, Belenus, Nidh\u00f6ggr). Many people are unhappy with it, but it's what we've got now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10624-sacerdos","name":"Sacerdos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10624_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"231"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T11:43:22-07:00","id":1412124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1412114-contradiction-between-titanomachy-and-mysteries-of-the-world#post1412114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Mysteries of the World Belenus and Cernunnos are described as gods. In Titanomachy they\u2019re described as Titans. I\u2019m confused. Are these two different beings with the same name or is this just supposed to point out how the line is blurry between gods and Titans?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given how it's explicit that there can be multiple facets of the same god with different personalities, I'd say that the Fomorian Belenus and Cernunnos are both facets of them associated with Donmu, but they also have parts of them that are still Gaulish Gods instead of Tuatha Titans.<br /> <br /> It is confusing, and a side effect of Donmu collecting strays and outcasts. Hell, it's suggested that Donmu and Danu are two different Mantles of the same God/Titan. It's a glorious mess, and one Titanomachy fully admits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T14:05:31-07:00","id":1412161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Nemetondevos were destroyed, with rare exception. A few survived in Britain until Rome conquered it a century later. Several lived on in different Mantles as members of neighboring pantheons or Titans craving vengeance. - Mysteries of the World, pg 38 </div> </div> </div>Gods of the Nemetondevos surviving as different Mantles, some of them Titanic, shouldn't come is a major surprise. Irish Cernunnos or Belenus (who says in his write-up that he grew in power under Roman rule) vs. Belenos (the fallen Nemetondevos) shouldn't be treated as any different than the Irish Gobannos that was already presented in the Nemetondevos write-up.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm still not 100% sold on the Nidhoggr the Titan vs N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggr the Dragon write-up, but I'm willing to withhold judgement on it until I can get my hands on Scion: Dragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4637,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","user":"demonchilde","date":". 09-05-2020, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4637-demonchilde","name":"demonchilde","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T15:14:52-07:00","id":1412169,"title":"","content":"I'd say they are different Mantles, though if they are separate beings is still up in air. Of course, I also add Watcher's Revised Nemetondevos, representing the original (dead and shattered) mantles, making the Mysteries of the World a revival of the Pantheon.<br /> As for Nidhoggr...he is not the only Titan in the book who also qualifies as a Dragon, though he is the only one called out as separate entity to said Dragon. Not sure if this will be explained when Dragon drops","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T15:37:51-07:00","id":1412174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1412114-contradiction-between-titanomachy-and-mysteries-of-the-world?p=1412169#post1412169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say they are different Mantles, though if they are separate beings is still up in air. Of course, I also add Watcher's Revised Nemetondevos, representing the original (dead and shattered) mantles, making the Mysteries of the World a revival of the Pantheon.<br /> As for Nidhoggr...he is not the only Titan in the book who also qualifies as a Dragon, though he is the only one called out as separate entity to said Dragon. Not sure if this will be explained when Dragon drops</div> </div> </div> </div>Titanomachy and Dragon were written during the same period of time, and Nidhoggr in both books were handled by the same author. So, yes! It will be explained <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.erykahfassett.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman, serif\"><b>Erykah Fassett</b></span></a><br /> <i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;The closer you get to the light, the greater your shadow becomes.&quot;</span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24398-shadowblossoms","name":"ShadowBlossoms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24398_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T16:24:18-07:00","id":1412181,"title":"","content":"Of course, some things might be holy and/or ineffable mysteries. This is a game of Myth and Wonder and the developers have already made it clear some questions won't get answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T17:29:07-07:00","id":1412189,"title":"","content":"&quot;So, what\u2019s the real answer? Is Apep both a dragon and a Titan in one being, or is Apophis the dragon and Apep the Titan serpent? Are they two individuals, or one individual playing two sides in an endless struggle, pitting dragons and Titans against each other?<br /> Again, the answer to all those questions might very simply be \u201cyes.\u201d That\u2019s up to the Storyguide\u2019s intentions for a specific chronicle. What looks like Apep and Apophis struggling over a single character\u2019s loyalties, arguing whether she\u2019s a Titan Scion or a dragon\u2019s child, or fighting with one another over a relic, might legitimately be what it seems: two individuals with very similar tastes and names fighting over the same handbag at a Nordstrom sale. On the other hand, perhaps those two individuals share and overlap, like Gentle Annie, The Morrigan and Badb sharing a single teenage body and swapping out perspectives.Perhaps Apep doesn\u2019t have full awareness of what Apophis does, and vice versa.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T18:33:05-07:00","id":1412195,"title":"","content":"I get it<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think it\u2019s a bad idea. I was just confused about whether it was two different people or two aspects of the same being. After reading it carefully, my personal headcanon is that Belenus is two aspects of the same being and Cernunnos is two diff people.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24398-shadowblossoms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24398_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24398\" data-vbnamecard=\"24398\">ShadowBlossoms</a> you\u2019re one of the writers. I liked Titanomachy and I can\u2019t wait for Dragons. And I love your sig \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T22:09:10-07:00","id":1412218,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25521_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25521\" data-vbnamecard=\"25521\">Spider</a> from cited quote - I get it right that both Titan Mantle and Dragon Mantle of the same being can fight each other? Like Apohis Titan will fight Dragon Apep?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T23:26:04-07:00","id":1412225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1412114-contradiction-between-titanomachy-and-mysteries-of-the-world?p=1412218#post1412218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25521_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25521\" data-vbnamecard=\"25521\">Spider</a> from cited quote - I get it right that both Titan Mantle and Dragon Mantle of the same being can fight each other? Like Apohis Titan will fight Dragon Apep?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe so. Certainly I feel the Titan Belenus would fight the God Belenos and vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-05T23:55:43-07:00","id":1412227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1412114-contradiction-between-titanomachy-and-mysteries-of-the-world?p=1412218#post1412218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25521_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25521\" data-vbnamecard=\"25521\">Spider</a> from cited quote - I get it right that both Titan Mantle and Dragon Mantle of the same being can fight each other? Like Apohis Titan will fight Dragon Apep?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep! The question is, are they separate beings? Are they two faces of the same being putting on a show (as someone pointed out above, there is implication that Domnu and Danu might be Mantles of the same being playing some long con)? Is there some third option I didn't think of when I was writing that section? It's up to the Storyguide. What makes the best sense for the story you're telling at your table? <br /> <br /> David Castro wrote some great stuff for Apep and Apophis and he'd be very sad if NO ONE made them fight each other. <br /> <br /> (Also Belenus would TOTALLY fight Belenos.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T02:36:33-07:00","id":1412239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1412114-contradiction-between-titanomachy-and-mysteries-of-the-world?p=1412227#post1412227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep! The question is, are they separate beings? Are they two faces of the same being putting on a show (as someone pointed out above, there is implication that Domnu and Danu might be Mantles of the same being playing some long con)? Is there some third option I didn't think of when I was writing that section? It's up to the Storyguide. What makes the best sense for the story you're telling at your table?<br /> <br /> David Castro wrote some great stuff for Apep and Apophis and he'd be very sad if NO ONE made them fight each other.<br /> <br /> (Also Belenus would TOTALLY fight Belenos.)</div> </div> </div> </div>(Winner gets a new Mantle, with fancy new Relics/Purview[s?] and maybe a new Calling)<br /> Things is, if Apep/Aphosis are the same being, they would fake the fight (with real collateral damage) just to throw off suspicious individuals, until they could use it to crush Re.<br /> The question is, were they always like this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 09-06-2020, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:11:39-07:00","id":1412276,"title":"","content":"The Demigod backer manuscript provides a fairly simple solution to such issues. If a god has multiple Mantles and dies, the Mantles are up for grabs. Any Scion who is sufficiently in tune with the Mantle can potentially become that god by performing appropriate legendary activities. So the two beings with similar names may once have been the same guy, but are now two new guys who rummaged through the old guy's wardrobe after he died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:57:03-07:00","id":1412285,"title":"","content":"There you go. A third thing I did not put in that section. That is essentially what happened with Ymir, though (as written in the book, anyway, you do what works for your game), all of his Mantles at that time went to the kid who got his heart from Jord. If his Mantles had been split up, there could easily be multiple Ymirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25521-spider","name":"Spider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25521_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-06T07:58:45-07:00","id":1412287,"title":"","content":"Expanding on Shepherdboi, let\u2019s say Cernunnos had a mantle more related to the wild and destructive side of nature and one linked to prosperity, when he died both mantels were abandoned and each one was taken by a different being, one that become a titan and one that is considered the reincarnation of the dead god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super 